{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ThbVrZwczZKAjtuZxaJZBT","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"B06\": {\n    \"gate\": \"G1\",\n    \"title\": \"Approval integrity\",\n    \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n    \"requirement\": \"Tie each approval to the agent instance that asked, and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope. Record who approved it and when it expires. Show the reviewer what the action will do. Make approvals single-use, or set clear limits on a broader grant. When the action runs, check permissions and the relevant resource state again. Record each use of an approval in one step, so parallel calls can't go past the grant. Test changed arguments, a different agent instance, expired approvals, replay, parallel reuse, and approvers without authority. If the approval service fails, the action must not quietly go ahead.\",\n    \"not_covered\": [\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A high-impact action that never asks for approval at all\",\n        \"owner\": \"B05\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A parent gaining a denied power by asking a stronger peer\",\n        \"owner\": \"E08\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"Harness or approval code changed in production without review\",\n        \"owner\": \"B12\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no actions that need approval under B05, with that inventory recorded.\",\n    \"checks\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"B06.1\",\n        \"check\": \"Each approval record is bound to the requesting agent instance and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope, and records the approver and an expiry time.\",\n        \"coverage_required\": true,\n        \"verify\": \"1) Find the approval data model (schema, class, table, `approval`). 2) List its fields. 3) Answer no if it lacks any of agent instance ID, operation, target, exact arguments or hash, scope, approver, and expiry, or if approval is a boolean like `approved=True`.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"B06.2\",\n        \"check\": \"When the action runs, the gate rejects it if the instance, operation, target, or arguments differ from the approval, or if the approval has expired.\",\n        \"coverage_required\": true,\n        \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approved action executes. 2) Check the code compares instance, operation, target, and arguments (or hash) against the stored approval and checks expiry at that moment. 3) Answer no if approval is checked only when requested, any field is not compared, arguments are re-read from the model after the check, or expiry is never checked.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"B06.3\",\n        \"check\": \"Each use of an approval is recorded in one atomic step (single-use or a bounded counter), so replays and parallel calls cannot go past the grant.\",\n        \"coverage_required\": true,\n        \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approval is used or marked consumed. 2) Check it is one atomic step: transaction with lock, compare-and-set, unique constraint, or atomic decrement. 3) Answer no if it reads then writes separately, never marks use, or keeps the count in process memory that parallel workers do not share.\"\n      },\n      {\n   skill/SKILL.md\n\nskill/heuristics:\nagent.yaml\nbuild-time.yaml\nconfiguration.yaml\necosystem.yaml\nrun-time.yaml\n\nskill/prescan:\npatterns.yaml\n\nskill/references:\nagent.md\nbuild-time.md\nchecks.json\nconfiguration.md\necosystem.md\nrun-time.md\n\nskill/scripts:\n__pycache__\nanswer.py\nchallenge.py\nmerge_findings.py\nnew_findings.py\nprescan.py\nreview_coverage.py\ntest_challenge.py\ntest_prescan.py\ntest_review_coverage.py\nvalidate_findings.py\nagent/infra/terraform/main.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/github.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/iam.tf\nagent/test/controls.test.ts\nagent/test/budget.test.ts\nagent/config/tools.allowlist.yaml\nagent/config/policy.yaml\nagent/config/budgets.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/release/manifest.json\nagent/brace-findings.json\nagent/README.md\nagent/package.json\nagent/.github/CODEOWNERS\nagent/.github/workflows/deploy.yml\nagent/.github/workflows/ci.yml\nagent/prompts/intent-classifier.txt\nagent/prompts/system.md\nagent/tsconfig.json\nagent/src/tools/executor.ts\nagent/src/tools/metadata-scan.ts\nagent/src/tools/registry.ts\nagent/src/tools/approvals.ts\nagent/src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts\nagent/src/agent/identity.ts\nagent/src/agent/context-size.ts\nagent/src/agent/loop.ts\nagent/src/agent/budget.ts\nagent/src/agent/classifier.ts\nagent/src/integrations/sms.ts\nagent/src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts\nagent/src/integrations/payments.ts\nagent/src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts\nagent/src/audit/recorder.ts\nagent/src/workers/reminders.ts\nagent/src/config.ts\nagent/src/server.ts\nagent/src/routes/webchat.ts\nagent/src/routes/sms-webhook.ts\nagent/src/control/kill-switch.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b7c8001-e55e-4973-a7ea-b20672c305f7","uuid":"aa18af20-dfd2-4630-a04b-450487baca6c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:41:10.719Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"B06\": {\n    \"gate\": \"G1\",\n    \"title\": \"Approval integrity\",\n    \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n    \"requirement\": \"Tie each approval to the agent instance that asked, and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope. Record who approved it and when it expires. Show the reviewer what the action will do. Make approvals single-use, or set clear limits on a broader grant. When the action runs, check permissions and the relevant resource state again. Record each use of an approval in one step, so parallel calls can't go past the grant. Test changed arguments, a different agent instance, expired approvals, replay, parallel reuse, and approvers without authority. If the approval service fails, the action must not quietly go ahead.\",\n    \"not_covered\": [\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A high-impact action that never