alls budget.recordUsage, so its tokens and cost are in no run, subject, tenant or fleet counter. countTokens (context-size.ts:35) is also unmetered, and the SDK retries once (loop.ts:15 maxRetries: 1) without counting. Agent calls are charged after the call (loop.ts:63), bounded only by max_tokens 1024 but with unbounded input size per turn.\"\nA B07.4 --met no --evidence src/agent/classifier.ts:45 --quote 'res = await client.messages.create(' --note \"Classifier and countTokens calls escape the per-subject, per-tenant and fleet cost quotas, so many small runs routed to staff are unmetered. No per-subject or per-service tool-call rate quota exists (budget.ts:160-161 are tenant and fleet only).\"\nA B08.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:35 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"' --note \"One runtime role reads every clinic's EHR, payments and SMS secrets, and the tenant is chosen by request data: webchat.ts:43 prefers the x-clinic-id header over the JWT claim, and executor.ts:63 takes clinicId from model tool input. Egress and hostNetwork are otherwise closed.\"\nA B08.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"Tenant isolation is enforced by agent code that model output steers. No infrastructure rule or check ties the clinicId to the caller's tenant.\"\nA B09.1 --met unknown --note \"NetworkPolicy at k8s/deployment.yaml:168-195 is default-deny with named peers, but the destination allowlist lives in the platform egress-proxy (comment at k8s/deployment.yaml:114-116), outside this repo.\"\nA B09.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 --quote 'const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));' --note \"The jku URL comes from the peer's unverified JWS header and is fetched before signature check, with no host allowlist