{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDbBUV7LjSq32GLMh76D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and rated all five as gaps. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I ran no challenges and added no other items.\n\n| Item | Gate | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | G1 | gap | `checkApproval` (`src/tools/approvals.ts:75-77`) never compares `argsHash` or `agentInstanceId`. The approval is never consumed (`src/tools/executor.ts:82`), so it can be replayed. The record has no scope field. Nothing rechecks permissions or resource state before the tool runs. |\n| B07 Hard execution budgets | G2 | gap | The Haiku classifier call (`src/agent/classifier.ts:45`) and `countTokens` are not charged to any cost or rate quota. There is no per-subject rate quota. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | G2 | gap | The runtime role reads every clinic's secrets (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:35`). The tenant is chosen by the `x-clinic-id` header (`src/routes/webchat.ts:43`) or by model-supplied `clinicId` (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`). |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | G2 | gap | `createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku))` (`src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83`) fetches a peer-supplied URL with no destination, resolved-IP or redirect check. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | G2 | gap | Provenance is generated in CI but never verified. The repo has no admission policy. |\n\n- **Passed or unknown checks:**\n  - Checks answered yes: B06.5, B07.1, B07.3, B08.1, B09.2, B10.1, B10.5.\n  - Checks answered unknown because the control sits outside the repo: B09.1, B09.4, B09.5, B10.2, B10.4.\n- **Prescan hits:** I dismissed H001–H005 with reasons. None of them belong to B06–B10 by item ID; I resolved them because they touch host isolation and credentials for B08. The pod securityContext sets the hardening fields, and the wildcard `Resource` in H005 is on `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` in the CI deploy role, not the agent's.\n- **Proxy use:** I noted but did not rate that Node `fetch` doesn't read `HTTPS_PROXY` and `src` has no `ProxyAgent`. The NetworkPolicy would then block calls to the model, payments and SMS providers.\n- **Model qualification:** `SKILL.md` says Sonnet isn't a qualified reviewer model. I recorded that in the scope.\n- **Hand edit:** I set `scope` and `repo` in the JSON by hand because `answer.py` has no way to set them.\n- **Scratch files:** My ledger row files are in `work/`. `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2218,"cache_read_input_tokens":99260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2218},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b7c8001-e55e-4973-a7ea-b20672c305f7","uuid":"eacdd83f-1cb3-4d3f-864e-32be5c983a33","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:45:22.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgDbBUB1R3411sgBDqzkY"}
